Package: aquaTrajectories
Title: Aquatic Animal Movement and Multiview Trajectories
Version: 0.0.35.9000
Authors@R: person("Stefanos", "Balaskas", email = "56984563+stefanosbalaskas@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Development-stage tools for validated two- and three-dimensional aquatic animal trajectories, movement and group metrics, event alignment, synchronization, and calibrated stereo geometry and observed 3D voxel occupancy, reviewer-gated cross-view hypotheses, and conditional pixel-error propagation. Provisional automatic geometric cross-camera identity hypotheses and a configured fish-video-to-refractive-3D software bridge are implemented using externally supplied camera calibration, clocks, and detector weights. Independently validated biological identities, underwater physical metrology, fish detector training, and externally certified measurement-error inference remain outstanding.
